*---------------------------------------------------------------
* sc.proc.equ -- maux's own process-call numbers (spawn/
* exit/wait/pipe/brk/pstat -- concepts the ProDOS MLI has NO
* equivalent for). Split out of inc/syscall.equ (task #8,
* docs/SELFHOST-CONVERSION.md phase 1) per docs/SYSCALL.md
* ruling on ABI FRICTION item 2 -- the call-number table was
* PUT whole by every compilation unit regardless of which half
* (process vs. file calls) it actually used, and PUT never
* reclaims (learning:01M0CC62FZ351EBXCAAKX52KAJ). Grouping
* DERIVED from a reference-set scan: liba/syscalls.s (the one
* choke point every userland program links) and the kernel's
* dispatch/spawn modules need this half; see
* inc/sc.file.equ for the other.
*
* `put`-only file (no code/org/dsk), same precondition
* discipline as memmap.equ -- the top-level file must `put`
* this directly.
*---------------------------------------------------------------

* -- maux PROCESS calls (no MLI equivalent) -- sequential,
* 1-based --
SYS_SPAWN   equ   1
SYS_EXIT    equ   2
SYS_WAIT    equ   3
SYS_PIPE    equ   4
SYS_BRK     equ   5
* REFACTOR POINT: SYS_PSTAT is the first call whose only job is
* to show kernel state to userland. If several such consumers
* ever want the SAME access pattern, build the /DEV namespace
* and retire this into it -- but not for a second call alone. A
* 6-byte record in a shared header is a SMALLER contract than a
* text format the kernel owns. See docs/SYSCALL.md section 10.
SYS_PSTAT   equ   6     ;read one PCB slot -- what ps is made of
* SYS_CLOCK -- copy the ProDOS Global Page's raw date/time
* words ($BF90-$BF93, ProDOS 8 TRM ch.6) to the caller. A maux
* PROCESS call, not a file call: no MLI opcode reads the clock
* (the global page is plain memory ANY program may read once
* it's mapped main -- see src/kernel/procfile.s's PRC_CLOCK
* header), so inc/sc.file.equ's "file syscall numbers
* ARE raw MLI opcodes" house rule does not apply here. `date`
* (docs/FLEET.md's "MISSING KERNEL FEATURE" line) is the first
* caller; task 2026-08-21.
SYS_CLOCK   equ   7
* SYS_FORK -- src/kernel/procfork.s. Takes NO parameter block
* (the register-carried parms pointer is ignored), returns the
* child's pid to the parent and 0 to the child, ERR_AGAIN when
* the bank free list is empty. It is 8 because this file's own
* grouping rule is "maux process calls keep small sequential
* numbers below MLI_RANGE_LO" and 1..7 above run sequentially --
* not because fork has any claim on that particular number.
* vfork stays DELETED (ARCHITECTURE.md: spawn subsumes it
* without the borrowed-bank UB rules).
SYS_FORK    equ   8

* -- SYS_DUP2 -- src/kernel/procfd2.s PRC_DUP2. dup2(oldfd,
* -- newfd): point one of the CALLER'S OWN fd slots at an
* -- already-open object. Two parameter bytes, oldfd then
* -- newfd; returns newfd.
* --
* -- Why it is a PROCESS call and not a file call: it rearranges
* -- PCB_FDTABLE, which is kernel bookkeeping. It never reaches
* -- ProDOS, so it has no MLI number to borrow and belongs in
* -- the small sequential range with spawn/fork/pipe.
* --
* -- The mechanism already existed: spawn()'s FDACT_DUP has done
* -- exactly this since fdactions landed, but only against the
* -- PARENT's table at spawn time, so a running process could
* -- never repoint its own fd. That gap is what blocked
* -- subshells (docs/SH-SUBSHELL.md) -- fork() was never the
* -- blocker. docs/SHELL-GAPS.md sec 1.
SYS_DUP2    equ   9

* -- SYS_TICK -- elapsed time, NOT wall time. Distinct from
* -- SYS_CLOCK (7) because a CLOCK and a TICK are different
* -- hardware and a machine can have either, both or neither
* -- (docs/SHELL-GAPS.md sec 5): a No-Slot Clock gives a date
* -- and no interrupt; an AppleMouse gives a 60 Hz interrupt and
* -- no date. A wall clock is also the wrong primitive for
* -- elapsed time at any resolution -- one that can be set
* -- backwards is not a stopwatch.
* --
* -- IT REPORTS THE MODE ALONGSIDE THE COUNT, and that is not
* -- decoration. src/kernel/timer.s's TIMER_MD_COOP arms no
* -- hardware source, so the counter does not advance SLOWLY in
* -- that mode, it never advances at all. A bare counter cannot
* -- tell a caller "no time has passed" from "time does not
* -- pass here", and a `sleep` that polls a frozen counter
* -- hangs forever.
SYS_TICK    equ   10

* -- SYS_FDSTAT -- src/kernel/procfd2.s PRC_FDSTAT. fdstat(fd):
* -- what KIND of object does one of the CALLER'S OWN fd slots
* -- hold. One parameter byte (the fd); returns the type in A.
* --
* -- This is maux's isatty(3)/gtty(2): V7 sh prompts only when
* -- its input is a TERMINAL, and no userland heuristic can make
* -- that call -- a tty and a pipe are both unseekable, and the
* -- fd table lives in the annex where no process can look
* -- (docs/SYSCALL.md sec 10's constraint). First caller is sh's
* -- interactive flag (docs/SHELL-GAPS.md sec 2): a $( ) child
* -- is a whole sh reading a pipe, and a prompt printed there
* -- sprays the console mid-substitution.
* --
* -- RESULT ENCODING: a DEVICE fd returns its raw table byte
* -- (>= FD_DEV_BASE, inc/sc.devfd.equ -- test the high
* -- bit and you have isatty). Anything else returns the FDST_*
* -- tag below. Closed fd or fd >= 8: carry set, ERR_INVAL.
SYS_FDSTAT  equ   11

* -- ttygeo(buf,fd): 4 mode bytes for a console fd -- see
* -- src/kernel/tty7.s PRC_TTYGEO + docs/VIDMODE.md sec 2.
SYS_TTYGEO  equ   12

* -- kill(pid, signo): terminate a process. THE SIGNO IS
* -- CARRIED, NOT DELIVERED: maux has no trap/handler machinery
* -- yet, so every nonzero signo terminates -- but the victim's
* -- wait status is $80|signo (the STATUS_INTR encoding: ^C is
* -- signal 2 = $82, kill's default 15 reaps $8F, -9 reaps $89),
* -- so the INT/TERM/KILL lanes are distinct in the ABI today
* -- and `trap` can make the default lane catchable later with
* -- no ABI change. Signo 0 is V7's liveness probe: validate the
* -- pid, kill nothing, carry says whether it lives. The victim
* -- becomes a zombie and its parent is woken; fds close at the
* -- parent's reap, the ^C sweep's own discipline (procspawn2.s
* -- PRC_INTR_SWP is this call's tick-context twin). kill(self)
* -- is exit($80|signo). Refused: pid 0, out-of-range, unused
* -- or zombie slots (ERR_SRCH), and the root tier -- a process
* -- with parent 0 (ERR_INVAL): killing a boot process orphans
* -- the console. The CONSOLE SHELL is killable (RULINGS-1,
* -- 2026-10-18: init respawns it). A killed process's own
* -- children are ADOPTED BY INIT at its death (ORPHAN-1, V7
* -- sys1.c / 4.2BSD kern_exit.c): PCB_PARENT := 1, a STOPPED
* -- one gets SIGHUP then SIGCONT through its own disposition,
* -- and init is woken for a zombie one.
SYS_KILL    equ   13

* -- signal(signo, action): set this process's disposition for
* -- one signal; returns the PREVIOUS action. Actions: SIGA_DFL
* -- terminate (today's kill), SIGA_IGN discard at the sender,
* -- SIGA_CATCH hold -- pending bit + ERR_INTR out of a blocked
* -- syscall; the process fetches with SYS_SIGPEND. NO handler
* -- addresses in v1 (refused ERR_INVAL, never stored as a
* -- promise delivery would break) -- the async-dispatch upgrade
* -- trigger is named in docs/SIGNALS.md sec 1. Dispositions are
* -- STICKY (A12: POSIX sigaction behaviour, not V7's
* -- reset-on-catch race -- sh reinstalls anyway, so no V7
* -- script can tell). Refused: signo 0, 9 (V7: SIGKILL "cannot
* -- be caught or ignored"), >15; action >2.
SYS_SIGNAL  equ   14
* -- sigpend(): pop the LOWEST pending held signo (fetch-and-
* -- clear), 0 = none. Lowest-first is V7 trap's own "executed
* -- in order of signal number". A maux-ism in the SYS_PSTAT
* -- tradition -- the honest surface for what V7 spelled
* -- as handler dispatch; docs/SIGNALS.md sec 2.
SYS_SIGPEND equ   15

* -- SYS_SIGNAL action values --
SIGA_DFL    equ   0
SIGA_IGN    equ   1
SIGA_CATCH  equ   2

* -- SIG_TSTP -- the cooperative-suspend signo (docs/JOB-CONTROL
* -- .md Increment E). A maux number: POSIX's 18 is outside the
* -- 1-15 signo space. Purely a DISPOSITION -- a process that
* -- SC_SIGNAL(SIG_TSTP, CATCH)s opts into handling ^Z itself
* -- (vi: rmcup + SYS_STOP + smcup); the ^Z sweep PRC_STOP_SWP
* -- delivers it to a catcher (pending + ERR_INTR) and
* -- direct-stops a non-catcher. It is not a SYS_KILL stop
* -- action -- `kill -14` still terminates, like every signo;
* -- the ^Z sweep is the only stop path.
SIG_TSTP    equ   14
SIG_HUP     equ   1                 ;V7 SIGHUP (ORPHAN-1)

* -- FDST_* -- SYS_FDSTAT's non-device result values. These MUST
* -- equal mm.annex.equ's OFT_PIPE_R/OFT_PIPE_W/OFT_FILE
* -- tags: the kernel returns its OFT_TYPE byte RAW rather than
* -- spending image bytes translating it, so these names are the
* -- userland spelling of the same numbers. check-process's
* -- fdstat cases assert each value through this header -- if
* -- the annex tags ever move, that gate goes red before any
* -- caller misreads a pipe as a file.
FDST_PIPE_R equ   1
FDST_PIPE_W equ   2
FDST_FILE   equ   3
* -- FDST_BLK: a /dev/sNdM block device fdstat tag -- docs/
* -- KSEG.md "Cells and equates".
FDST_BLK    equ   4

* -- ttymode(fd, newflags) = SYS_TTYMODE -- src/kernel/tty7.s
* -- PRC_TTYMODE. SET the target console's mode flags, RETURN
* -- THE PREVIOUS flags (the signal()/SYS_SIGNAL shape, so a
* -- caller can save+restore -- docs/VI-DESIGN.md's stty(1)).
* -- Three orthogonal bits, deliberately not V7's full raw-no-
* -- signal ladder (that is out of scope for this seed): ICANON
* -- (line discipline: cook to CR with erase/kill editing), ECHO
* -- (paint typed bytes), and OPOST (VT102 slice 1,
* docs/CONSOLE-
* -- VT102.md sec 3, the GNO/ME CRMOD precedent -- learning:
* -- 01M287MW1Y9Q719BAYFTN4C5M8): a CR ($8D, maux's own line
* -- terminator) reaching the TERMINAL layer becomes a full
* -- newline (column 0 + index) when OPOST is set, and moves the
* -- column only, strict VT102, when it is clear. cooked default
* =
* -- all three set. ^C stays a signal in EVERY mode -- it is
* -- intercepted upstream of the ring (tty3.s TTY_KEYIN), never
* -- gated by any of these bits. Same fd rules as SYS_TTYGEO:
* -- >= FD_DEV_BASE and <= FD_TTY3, else ERR_INVAL.
TMD_ICANON  equ   1
TMD_ECHO    equ   2
TMD_OPOST   equ   4
SYS_TTYMODE equ   16

* -- tcsetfg(&job) = SYS_TCSETFG -- src/kernel/procspawn2.s
* -- PRC_TCSETFG (docs/JOB-CONTROL.md, Increment A). The shell
* -- DECLARES its console's FOREGROUND JOB: the parm block is
* -- {count, pid0, pid1, pid2} (count 0 = idle prompt, nothing
* -- is foreground). ^C on that console then kills exactly that
* -- job -- the set's live pids and their descendants -- instead
* -- of the old "every process at spawn depth >= 3 on the whole
* -- machine" sweep. The console is the CALLER's fd 0 (a tty
* -- device fd, else ERR_INVAL). SET-TIME HARDENING: count <=
* -- TCSETFG_MAX and every pid a CHILD of the caller or the
* -- CALLER ITSELF (a raw-mode shell declares itself while it
* -- reads, so ^C/^Z reach it as signals), else ERR_INVAL --
* -- the only caller is a shell naming its own children. The
* -- kernel scrubs a reaped pid out of every set
* -- (PRC_FG_SCRUB), so a stale entry can never name a reused
* -- pid. TCSETFG_MAX is sh's MAXCMD (a pipeline is <= 3
* -- stages); sh asserts the two agree.
SYS_TCSETFG equ   17
TCSETFG_MAX equ   3

* -- cont(pid) = SYS_CONT -- src/kernel/procsig.s PRC_CONT
* -- (docs/JOB-CONTROL.md Increment B): resume a STOPPED child.
* -- The SIGCONT equivalent, and deliberately NOT a signo of
* -- SYS_KILL: maux's signal model is "every nonzero signo
* -- terminates" (docs/SIGNALS.md sec 1) and a continue is not a
* -- termination. STOPPED -> RUNNABLE + run queue, wait channel
* -- cleared -- PRC_SIG_SND's blocked-wake, applied to the one
* -- state it never touches. Refused ERR_INVAL unless the pid is
* -- a CHILD of the caller (the SYS_TCSETFG hardening) AND is
* -- PCB_STOPPED right now.
SYS_CONT    equ   18

* -- waitjob(&status2, flags) = SYS_WAITJOB -- src/kernel/
* -- process2.s PRC_WAITJOB, sharing PRC_WAIT's reap core. The
* -- job-control wait: flags WJ_NOHANG (poll: return 0 instead
* -- of blocking when no child is ready) and WJ_UNTRACED (report
* -- a STOPPED child too -- reported, never reaped). Writes a
* -- TWO-BYTE {kind, code} to the buffer: WJ_EXITED + exit
* -- status, WJ_SIGNALED + signo (the $80|signo status decoded),
* -- WJ_STOPPED + 0. Why two bytes and not V7's $7F: a one-byte
* -- status already means exit 127 there. Returns the pid in A;
* -- 0 = WJ_NOHANG and nothing ready; carry + ERR_CHILD when the
* -- caller has no children, OR when every child is STOPPED and
* -- WJ_UNTRACED was not asked for -- nothing could ever wake
* -- that sleep. The legacy SYS_WAIT (1-byte status, blocks,
* -- reaps ZOMBIE only) is unchanged and shares the same rule
* -- for an all-stopped child set. REPORT-ONCE INVARIANT
* -- (gated): WJ_UNTRACED reports a stop on EVERY call while
* -- the child stays stopped -- the one sanctioned consumer is
* -- a blocking `fg` loop that consumes it and returns; a
* -- prompt-time poll uses WJ_NOHANG WITHOUT WJ_UNTRACED.
SYS_WAITJOB equ   19
WJ_NOHANG   equ   $01
WJ_UNTRACED equ   $02
WJ_EXITED   equ   0
WJ_SIGNALED equ   1
WJ_STOPPED  equ   2

* -- stop() = SYS_STOP -- src/kernel/process2.s PRC_STOP (docs/
* -- JOB-CONTROL.md Increment E): the caller parks ITSELF
* -- PCB_STOPPED until a SYS_CONT resumes it, waking its parent
* -- first (SCH_WAKEUP on PCB_PARENT) so a fg-waiting shell's
* -- SYS_WAITJOB sees the stop. SCH_SLEEP's shape with STOPPED
* -- for BLOCKED and no retry-rewind (a continue is not an
* -- interrupt): it RETURNS 0 when continued. The catcher's half
* -- of cooperative ^Z -- vi calls it between rmcup and smcup.
* -- No parameters.
SYS_STOP    equ   20

* -- SYS_VCSTAT -- which virtual consoles already have a shell.
* -- src/kernel/procfile3.s PRC_VCSTAT. Two parameter bytes, the
* -- caller's buffer pointer; VC_COUNT bytes are written there,
* -- one per console (console 1 is byte 0): the pid attached to
* -- that console, or 0 for none.
* --
* -- It exists for lazy consoles (docs/COVER-OFF.md): `chvt N`
* -- must not drop a person onto a console nobody reads, and
* -- must not stack a SECOND shell on one that already has one.
* -- ATTACHMENT is the property, not blocking. "Is somebody
* -- asleep on TTY_RD_CHAN+N" is true only while that shell sits
* -- at its prompt and false for the whole time it is running a
* -- command -- which is exactly when a person switches away and
* -- comes back. fd 0's object byte is FD_DEV_BASE+console for a
* -- console-attached process in BOTH states, and it is how
* -- PRC_TCSETFG already identifies the caller's console.
SYS_VCSTAT  equ   21

* -- SYS_HALT -- stop the world. procfile3.s PRC_HALT.
* -- ONE parameter byte, the mode; HALT_DOWN is the only one
* -- defined, and the byte exists so `bye`'s suspend mode can
* -- join it without renumbering.
* --
* -- IT DOES NOT RETURN. There is no error path and no result:
* -- by the time the mode byte has been read, every open file is
* -- closed, the periodic interrupt source is disarmed and the
* -- glass belongs to the motherboard again. A caller that wants
* -- to say something to the person says it BEFORE calling, and
* -- `shutdown` does.
* --
* -- WHAT IT DOES NOT PROMISE, said here because the promise is
* -- easy to assume: it flushes the KERNEL's files, not each
* -- process's userland stdio buffer, which lives in that
* -- process's own bank and can only be flushed by code running
* -- there. Unix has the same property for a SIGKILLed process.
* -- Utilities that buffer and are killed mid-write lose the
* -- tail; utilities that exit normally have already flushed.
SYS_HALT    equ   22
HALT_DOWN   equ   0    ;halt: quiesce and stop. Ctrl-Reset
                       ;reboots from here -- maux never took
                       ;$03F2 ($0300 is reserved for a reset
                       ;chain and nothing writes it), so the
                       ;ROM/ProDOS path is still intact and
                       ;"safe to reset" is a fact rather than
                       ;a hope. check-shutdown asserts it.

* -- SYS_BYE -- save+destroy+restore round trip (docs/
* -- BYE-SLICE1.md), PRC_BYE (src/kernel/procbye.s). No
* -- parameters in this slice. IT DOES NOT RETURN THE WAY IT
* -- WAS CALLED: the machine round-trips through a real MLI
* -- QUIT before the caller sees A again, but the call still
* -- behaves like an ordinary syscall to the caller -- returns
* -- with A = 0, no error path (allocating the save bank the
* -- first time can fail, and THAT failure returns normally,
* -- via ERR_NOMEM, with the round trip never attempted).
SYS_BYE     equ   23

* -- SYS_DEVLIST -- src/kernel/procfile4.s PRC_DEVLIST
* -- (docs/DEVFS.md, 2026-09-30). Copies out DEVCNT+1 bytes, one
* -- per DEVLST entry, DSSS in the high nibble ($F0-masked,
* -- learning:01KW1GTYH4NRG0F8M7AAT6EG9Z) with bit 0 SET when
* -- that unit's DEVADR ($BF10-$BF2F, indexed by the same DSSS
* -- nibble) falls in main LC bank 1 $D000-$D5FF -- the built-in
* -- Disk ][ driver (learning:01M0W5ZCYJQH2A19V5XJW2HZR4). NO
* -- device is touched: this is a pure global-page read, the
* -- whole point being that `/dev` costs nothing on a machine
* -- with an empty 5.25" drive (operator ruling, "never poll a
* -- 5.25-inch drive to list anything"). One parameter: the
* -- caller's buffer pointer (no leading count byte -- a maux
* -- call, not an MLI one). Returns the byte count (DEVCNT+1) in
* -- A on success.
SYS_DEVLIST equ   24

* -- SYS_VROOT (docs/VROOT.md): parm {op, ptr(2), arg}.
* -- op 0 = row (arg = index), 1 = mount (arg = unit),
* -- 2 = umount (arg = unit, ptr = "/NAME"), 3 = phys path
* -- (comes back at ptr), 4 = LOOPATT (ptr = image path, arg
* -- = host unit | -r | re-attach bits; play image only),
* -- 5 = CLASSIFY (ptr = a path; A = 0 an ordinary path,
* -- $80 "/", $81 "/dev", $82 "/mnt" once the cwd, "." and
* -- ".." are resolved; play image only, KFIX9).
SYS_VROOT   equ   25

* -- SYS_SLPUNTIL: parm = 4-byte ABSOLUTE tick count; blocks
* -- until the tick counter reaches it (procfile3.s, SLEEP-1).
SYS_SLPUNTIL equ 26

* -- $1B-$64 deliberately unassigned -- room to grow without
* renegotiating -- MLI_RANGE_LO (src/kernel/entry.s).
